{"seconds": 42.2, "exit": 0, "final": "Black's options are to capture the knight (Kxf6 or Qxf6) or take the pawn (Qxd5). Either way, White has won the knight on e4 and traded the f6 knight for Black's material. This is clearly winning.\n\n**Best move: Nf6+**\n\nThis is a fork - the knight checks the king while attacking the undefended knight on e4. After the forced king move, White plays Qxe4, winning material.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Nf6+\", \"line\": [\"Nf6+\", \"Kg7\", \"Qxe4\", \"Qxf6\", \"Qxf6\", \"Kxf6\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\"]}\n```\n\n---\n\n**Coaching Note:**\n\nYour knight on e4 was loose (undefended). Always scan for **forks**\u2014moves where one piece attacks two targets at once. Here, Nf6+ checks the king AND attacks your knight. You must respond to the check first, leaving the knight undefended for capture. Look for undefended enemy pieces, then ask: \"Can I force my opponent to move before capturing it?\" Forks that give check are especially deadly because the check takes priority.", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/2p2q2/1p1p2p1/1P1P4/1P2n1N1/r7/6QP/6RK w - - 0 37"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/2p2q2/1p1p2p1/1P1P4/1P2n1N1/r7/6QP/6RK w - - 0 37"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/2p2q2/1p1p2p1/1P1P4/1P2n1N1/r7/6QP/6RK w - - 0 37", "square": "g2"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/2p2q2/1p1p2p1/1P1P4/1P2n1N1/r7/6QP/6RK w - - 0 37", "square": "g4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/2p2q2/1p1p2p1/1P1P4/1P2n1N1/r7/6QP/6RK w - - 0 37", "square": "g1"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/2p2q2/1p1p2p1/1P1P4/1P2n1N1/r7/6QP/6RK w - - 0 37", "square": "f7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/2p2q2/1p1p2p1/1P1P4/1P2n1N1/r7/6QP/6RK w - - 0 37", "square": "f8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-square_info", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/2p2q2/1p1p2p1/1P1P4/1